  "mechanismSummary": "Ethoxide removes a proton from the CH₂ between the two esters of diethyl malonate. The stabilised enolate adds to the terminal carbon of methyl vinyl ketone (a Michael, or conjugate, addition), pushing the charge onto the ketone oxygen. Ethanol protonates this new enolate on carbon, regenerating ethoxide and giving diethyl 2-(3-oxobutyl)malonate.",
